Article 261

The immovable and movable property of a farmer collective are collectively owned by the members of this collective.
The following matters shall be decided by the collective's members in accordance with statutory procedures:
(1)	land contracting schemes, and the contracting of land to any organization or individual outside this collective;
(2)	adjustment to the contracted land among the persons who have the right to contractual management of land;
(3)	methods for the use and distribution of funds such as land compensation fees;
(4)	matters such as changes in the ownership of enterprises invested by the collective; and
(5)	other matters as provided by law.

translated_text:
Article 261

The immovable and movable property of a rural collective economic organization is collectively owned by the members of the collective.
The following matters shall be decided by the members of the collective in accordance with the legally prescribed procedures:
(1) land contracting plans and the contracting of land to units or individuals outside the collective;
(2) adjustment of contracted land among members with land contractual management rights;
(3) the use and distribution of funds such as land compensation fees;
(4) changes in the ownership of collectively invested enterprises and other matters;
(5) other matters prescribed by law.

Article 262

The ownership of collectively-owned land, forests, mountain ridges, grasslands, unreclaimed land, tidal flats, etc., shall be exercised in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) where they belong to the rural collective economic organization of a village, the collective economic organization of the village or the villagers' committee shall exercise ownership on behalf of the collective in accordance with law;
(2) where they belong to two or more rural collective economic organizations within a village, the respective collective economic organizations or villagers' groups shall exercise ownership on behalf of the collective in accordance with law;
(3) where they belong to the rural collective economic organization of a township (town), the collective economic organization of the township (town) shall exercise ownership on behalf of the collective.

